      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pittsboro%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors William Pitt the Younger, son of the Earl of Chatham, after whom the county is named.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pittsboro%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1881 a new courthouse and jail were built, and the historic traffic circle around the courthouse still marks the town center.",
